-- title:
--   Packed integer data for a finite prime-shift convolution
-- statement:
--   Three explicit nonnegative integers $Q_*,R_*,W_*$ are supplied as base-$2^{64}$ data, with128 digits per chunk. They are intended to encode a prime-position indicator, its reversal, and reversed singular weights for $D=40907$. Their identification with the original8000-prime family and lookup table is a separate theorem obligation. The definitions alone assert neither this identification nor the resulting finite pair-sum bound.
-- source:
